-- NORM-LOG N10 goal A: the IL-hvac menu redrafted as one chain per party (NORM-LOG-SPEC §7 N10).
-- Pass: FULFILLED on all three traces, and the official record in time order:
-- 1, 2, 1 (I1 P2 I3 T5); 2, 1 (P1 I2 T5); 1, 2, 1, 2 (I1 P2 I3 P4 T5). Before A it was member-major.
IMPORT prelude
DECLARE Who IS ONE OF I, P, T
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF a, b, done

-- The IL-hvac menu redrafted: one chain per party, so a matched act re-enters
-- only its own party's chain, and T's `done` closes the whole menu.
GIVEN d IS A Who
      act IS AN Act
GIVETH DEONTIC Who Act
`after` MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN I THEN COMMIT `seen` IS 1 HENCE `chain of` d
    OTHERWISE   COMMIT `seen` IS 2 HENCE `chain of` d

GIVEN d IS A Who
GIVETH DEONTIC Who Act
`chain of` MEANS
    PARTY d
    MAY    act
    WITHIN 100
    HENCE  `after` d act

GIVETH DEONTIC Who Act
menu MEANS
       (EVERY d IN LIST I, P
            MAY    act
            WITHIN 100
            UPON   EACH
            HENCE  `after` d act)
  ROR  (PARTY T MAY done WITHIN 100)

#TRACE menu AT 0 WITH  PARTY I DOES a AT 1   PARTY P DOES b AT 2   PARTY I DOES a AT 3   PARTY T DOES done AT 5
#TRACE menu AT 0 WITH  PARTY P DOES b AT 1   PARTY I DOES a AT 2   PARTY T DOES done AT 5
#TRACE menu AT 0 WITH  PARTY I DOES a AT 1   PARTY P DOES b AT 2   PARTY I DOES a AT 3   PARTY P DOES b AT 4  PARTY T DOES done AT 5
